Z||000003||Bazooka||09-29-2001||11:33 PM||||***************************<BR>Voyager,<BR>4T80E has been designed to take the Horsepower and Torque of the Northstar Engine (+ or - 300hp). I say that's your best bet for V8. The N'star conversion guys speak very highly of it. The only drawback is that it is much heavier than the Fiero 125c, but thats a small price for reliability. You can give 'Roadmaster Transmissions' a call since they build Racing Transmissions for 700hp + cars. They are at (847) 352-4557 and their website is at <A HREF="http://www.roadmastertranz.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.roadmastertranz.com/</A>  Bill Anthony is the specialist and mechanic who evaluated my Transmission dilemma. Feel free to ask him about my 350 TPI Black Fiero GT.<P>*****************************<BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by voyagerspe:<BR><B>I toasted my 125 today. what is the strongest auto I can fit in my fiero? It will be powered by a 350 tpi motor.im not really interested in a 4 speed but if its stronger i could go that route.  im considring a jpt 125 that archie recommends but "bazooka" states his had to be rebuilt 5 times and that has me looking for alteratives.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>****************************<P>||||reg||1
